# Commands run by the launchd job com.redwood.demo (see com.redwood.demo.plist).
# The switcher of running applications (RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.switcher, gpu=1): three applications are
# started one after another (ones that ask nothing: an application that puts up a question of its
# own -- Photos asks about notifications -- leaves a modal alert on the screen, and with one of
# those up iOS opens no switcher at all), the first two left running by the home button and the
# third kept on the screen; then a drag up from the bottom edge that stops a third of the way and
# waits opens the switcher, where the cards behind the front one are dimmed. Those of the two on
# the left came out purple instead. (If the drag brings nothing, the notification asks SpringBoard
# itself: see switcher() in inject_sb.c.)
# The first minute and a half after the boot the four cores are busy with the start-up's own work
# and an application started then takes much longer than it should (see rc.jobs.fps): the taps
# wait for it to be over.
/redwood/bin/sound_test springboard
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 25 swipe 0.5 0.985 0.5 0.3 200 wait 70
/redwood/bin/rwtouch tap 0.151 0.358 wait 20 button home wait 8
/redwood/bin/rwtouch tap 0.383 0.358 wait 20 button home wait 8
/redwood/bin/rwtouch tap 0.614 0.481 wait 20
/redwood/bin/rwtouch drag 0.5 0.995 0.5 0.62 600 2500 wait 8
/redwood/bin/rwtouch notify com.redwood.layers wait 30
# And what the wallpaper left on the volume for the frosted materials to take their bottom layer
# from: PaperBoardUI asks its source for a snapshot or a blurred copy, by image or by file name.
/var/jb/usr/bin/find /var -maxdepth 7 -iname "*allpaper*" -ls
/var/jb/usr/bin/find /var -maxdepth 7 -iname "*oster*" -ls
